## The Bug

The issue is that `Array.prototype.forEach` does **not** await Promises. Even though the callback is `async`, `forEach` calls it and immediately moves on to the next element without waiting for the Promise to resolve. By the time `forEach` finishes, the `out` array is still empty (or only partially filled), and the function returns before any of the `fetch` calls have completed.

## The Fix

Use `Promise.all` with `map` (or a `for...of` loop) so that the function actually waits for all fetches to complete before returning.

